1
00:00:04,637 --> 00:00:07,073
Two months until the Hakone Ekiden.

2
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:09,242
The Student United Team,
made up of runners from teams

3
00:00:09,309 --> 00:00:12,012
that failed to qualify, begins training.

4
00:00:12,078 --> 00:00:14,748
My goal is a top-three finish
at the Hakone Ekiden.

5
00:00:14,814 --> 00:00:16,016
A top-three finish?

6
00:00:16,082 --> 00:00:19,619
Some resist Coach Masato Kai's
unconventional methods,

7
00:00:19,686 --> 00:00:20,987
as he has no coaching experience.

8
00:00:21,054 --> 00:00:22,922
You'd be crazy to take this seriously!

9
00:00:22,989 --> 00:00:24,991
Don't mess with me!

10
00:00:25,058 --> 00:00:26,760
We've lost once already!

11
00:00:26,826 --> 00:00:28,762
That's exactly why
we can run like no one else!

12
00:00:28,828 --> 00:00:30,930
Meanwhile, at Dainichi TV…

13
00:00:30,997 --> 00:00:33,900
This is what we call
the Hakone Ekiden Broadcast Handbook.

14
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:36,936
It's essentially a manual
for broadcasting the Hakone Ekiden.

15
00:00:37,003 --> 00:00:41,074
Chief producer Ryo Tokushige
clashed with upper management.

16
00:00:41,141 --> 00:00:43,309
Hakone Ekiden belongs to the runners.

17
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:46,146
Perfectionist broadcast director

18
00:00:46,713 --> 00:00:48,915
Natsuki Miyamoto also clashed
with her crew.

19
00:00:48,982 --> 00:00:50,617
Is the broadcast director
some kind of god?

20
00:00:50,683 --> 00:00:53,586
Maybe I'm not cut out for this job.

21
00:00:53,653 --> 00:00:55,188
Maybe don't toss it all,

22
00:00:55,955 --> 00:00:56,990
but try tossing a little?

23
00:00:57,057 --> 00:00:59,092
-I'll go!
-Please go.

24
00:00:59,159 --> 00:01:00,460
Meanwhile…

25
00:01:00,527 --> 00:01:02,929
Maeda will probably be hospitalized.

26
00:01:03,663 --> 00:01:08,101
Another ordeal awaited those
already facing adversity.

27
00:01:08,168 --> 00:01:09,636
This is bad…

28
00:01:17,043 --> 00:01:20,880
CHIEF PRODUCER
RYO TOKUSHIGE

29
00:01:20,947 --> 00:01:22,248
What about the evening news?

30
00:01:22,315 --> 00:01:24,684
For now, the weekday sub-anchors

31
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:26,352
can fill in.

32
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,288
But going forward…

33
00:01:28,354 --> 00:01:29,189
ANNOUNCING DIRECTOR
PUBLIC RELATIONS DIRECTOR

34
00:01:29,255 --> 00:01:30,090
DEPUTY NEWS DIRECTOR

35
00:01:30,156 --> 00:01:31,091
Come in.

36
00:01:31,157 --> 00:01:32,826
Excuse me.

37
00:01:34,227 --> 00:01:35,328
Sorry I'm late.

38
00:01:35,395 --> 00:01:37,397
PROGRAMMING BUREAU CHIEF
TAKESHI KUROISHI

39
00:01:39,399 --> 00:01:42,001
Is Maeda going to be okay?

40
00:01:42,569 --> 00:01:46,139
Esophageal cancer. Stage three.

41
00:01:47,173 --> 00:01:48,775
Stage three…

42
00:01:49,709 --> 00:01:52,312
The Hakone Ekiden is just
two months away, isn't it?

43
00:01:52,378 --> 00:01:54,614
Who's going to fill in?

44
00:01:55,582 --> 00:01:57,150
Someone to replace Maeda…

45
00:01:58,017 --> 00:02:00,987
No, I really can't think of anyone.

46
00:02:01,054 --> 00:02:03,123
More than 20 announcers

47
00:02:03,189 --> 00:02:05,692
work on the Hakone Ekiden broadcast.

48
00:02:05,758 --> 00:02:09,162
The broadcast announcer leads

49
00:02:09,229 --> 00:02:11,664
the play-by-play announcers in the field.

50
00:02:11,731 --> 00:02:13,600
The command center, so to speak.

51
00:02:13,666 --> 00:02:17,303
It's no exaggeration to say
their skill decides

52
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:18,571
whether the broadcast succeeds.

53
00:02:18,638 --> 00:02:20,573
SHIRAKAWA HOSPITAL

54
00:02:21,141 --> 00:02:22,075
Mr. Tokushige,

55
00:02:22,809 --> 00:02:24,110
I'm so sorry.

56
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:26,179
Don't worry about it.

57
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:29,048
Besides that, how are you feeling?

58
00:02:29,649 --> 00:02:33,419
I just feel a little off.

59
00:02:34,454 --> 00:02:37,924
But now I'm starting radiation and chemo.

60
00:02:39,392 --> 00:02:40,527
I see.

61
00:02:41,628 --> 00:02:45,698
I was really looking forward
to doing Hakone with this team.

62
00:02:45,765 --> 00:02:46,799
HISASHI MAEDA

63
00:02:49,602 --> 00:02:50,770
I'm so frustrated…

64
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:54,407
Me too.

65
00:02:55,808 --> 00:02:59,412
Right now, your job
is to focus on getting better.

66
00:03:00,446 --> 00:03:03,082
When you're well, we'll do it again.

67
00:03:04,551 --> 00:03:05,451
Okay.

68
00:03:06,786 --> 00:03:08,555
Um, Mr. Tokushige.

69
00:03:09,088 --> 00:03:12,325
What's going to happen
about my replacement?

70
00:03:14,627 --> 00:03:15,728
I'll think about it.

71
00:03:16,896 --> 00:03:22,068
It's not my place to say,
but without enough time to prepare,

72
00:03:22,135 --> 00:03:26,072
Hakone will be tough for anyone
without real experience.

73
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:29,042
You're right.

74
00:03:30,910 --> 00:03:36,115
Well… It's not like I have no one in mind.

75
00:03:37,250 --> 00:03:38,284
Mr. Karashima?

76
00:03:43,723 --> 00:03:47,560
I was thinking the same thing.
I hope he will do it.

77
00:03:49,996 --> 00:03:52,865
Yeah, I know…

78
00:03:52,932 --> 00:03:55,635
Mr. Karashima?
You mean that Mr. Karashima?!

79
00:03:55,702 --> 00:03:57,971
Come on, Mr. Tokushige. Are you serious?

80
00:03:58,037 --> 00:03:59,739
You know what he's like.

81
00:03:59,806 --> 00:04:01,541
This is bad.

82
00:04:02,275 --> 00:04:03,409
Um, sorry.

83
00:04:03,476 --> 00:04:06,479
Is Mr. Karashima really that bad?

84
00:04:08,681 --> 00:04:10,283
He's really that bad.

85
00:04:10,350 --> 00:04:13,653
Basically, he's a pain.

86
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:16,756
He expects the crew
to know more than the experts.

87
00:04:16,823 --> 00:04:19,325
Plenty of directors have run from him.

88
00:04:19,392 --> 00:04:21,227
He chewed me out once too.

89
00:04:21,294 --> 00:04:23,029
"There’s no such phrase
as 'fixed concept'."

90
00:04:23,096 --> 00:04:24,964
"It's either 'fixed idea'
or 'preconception'."

91
00:04:25,031 --> 00:04:26,099
Could you say that again?

92
00:04:28,401 --> 00:04:30,737
I said, "Sorry, I should've studied more."

93
00:04:30,803 --> 00:04:32,538
"Not sorry. I'm sorry."

94
00:04:32,605 --> 00:04:35,842
"Can't you even apologize properly?"
And that set him off again.

95
00:04:35,908 --> 00:04:37,343
I'm traumatized.

96
00:04:37,410 --> 00:04:41,014
He handled my new-hire training too.

97
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:44,417
He drilled me for two hours
on how I pronounce my own name.

98
00:04:44,484 --> 00:04:45,351
Two hours?!

99
00:04:45,418 --> 00:04:48,621
He's got all three Hs.
Harsh, hard-nosed and hard to please.

100
00:04:48,688 --> 00:04:50,923
And he never takes a job he doesn't like.

101
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:52,659
How does that even work?

102
00:04:52,725 --> 00:04:55,061
Office workers are supposed to
do the jobs they're given.

103
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:57,163
50 DAYS UNTIL HAKONE EKIDEN

104
00:04:57,230 --> 00:04:58,665
I'm for it.

105
00:05:00,066 --> 00:05:02,669
Mr. Karashima is a pro at golf broadcasts.

106
00:05:02,735 --> 00:05:05,972
He's suited to Hakone,
where the competition happens all at once.

107
00:05:10,677 --> 00:05:13,346
Well, only those of us inside

108
00:05:13,413 --> 00:05:15,481
know how nasty he is.

109
00:05:16,015 --> 00:05:18,351
On air, he sounds smooth,

110
00:05:18,418 --> 00:05:21,321
and somehow he never comes off as snide.

111
00:05:21,387 --> 00:05:23,056
Is that praise or an insult?

112
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:28,027
He's hard to work with, sure.
But if we put up with that,

113
00:05:28,094 --> 00:05:31,731
I think… it'll be a great broadcast.

114
00:05:32,298 --> 00:05:34,834
-You think?
-But can you put up with him,

115
00:05:35,935 --> 00:05:37,170
Mr. Tokushige?

116
00:05:39,105 --> 00:05:40,006
Anyway,

117
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:41,941
no time like the present.

118
00:05:42,442 --> 00:05:44,344
TATEYAMA LADIES OPEN

119
00:05:58,157 --> 00:05:59,158
Mr. Karashima,

120
00:05:59,959 --> 00:06:01,027
it's been a while.

121
00:06:02,428 --> 00:06:05,898
On the final day,
they'll put the pin by this pond.

122
00:06:07,266 --> 00:06:09,836
This hole decides the tournament.

123
00:06:12,171 --> 00:06:13,039
Okay…

124
00:06:15,274 --> 00:06:16,609
What do you want?

125
00:06:19,412 --> 00:06:23,282
Actually, I have a favor to ask.

126
00:06:24,650 --> 00:06:27,887
Would you cover the Hakone Ekiden?

127
00:06:29,389 --> 00:06:31,691
Why not let one of the young ones do it?

128
00:06:34,327 --> 00:06:35,795
If someone young does it,

129
00:06:36,696 --> 00:06:39,132
I want to give them time to prepare.

130
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:41,834
You know me.

131
00:06:42,502 --> 00:06:46,773
I can't stand sappy sports broadcasts.

132
00:06:50,309 --> 00:06:52,311
15 YEARS AGO

133
00:06:52,378 --> 00:06:56,082
Mr. Karashima, could you tell
this story about the runner's family next?

134
00:06:56,783 --> 00:06:58,418
FAMILY STORY

135
00:06:58,985 --> 00:07:00,887
Sorry. Not now.

136
00:07:02,255 --> 00:07:05,057
-Hey, Tokushige!
-Yes!

137
00:07:05,124 --> 00:07:06,893
The family story's set, right?

138
00:07:06,959 --> 00:07:08,594
Next is Car Three.

139
00:07:08,661 --> 00:07:10,963
Uh, I'm sorry, but…

140
00:07:11,030 --> 00:07:14,100
Mr. Karashima doesn't seem willing to…

141
00:07:14,167 --> 00:07:16,702
What? Hey!

142
00:07:17,336 --> 00:07:20,106
Is he griping again?

143
00:07:20,173 --> 00:07:22,041
If not now, when?

144
00:07:22,108 --> 00:07:22,942
Shut up, Kitamura!

145
00:07:23,009 --> 00:07:24,644
You're annoying, Kitamura!

146
00:07:24,710 --> 00:07:26,312
What are you even watching?

147
00:07:26,379 --> 00:07:28,214
Look at the runner's head!

148
00:07:28,281 --> 00:07:31,551
It's swaying side to side.
That means he's tired.

149
00:07:31,617 --> 00:07:33,419
This is where the race is decided!

150
00:07:33,486 --> 00:07:34,720
And you're forcing a link

151
00:07:34,787 --> 00:07:39,659
between his family's tragedy
and his running?

152
00:07:39,725 --> 00:07:42,728
"His father is cheering him on
from heaven"?

153
00:07:42,795 --> 00:07:45,364
What is that? That's ridiculous!

154
00:07:45,932 --> 00:07:48,501
It doesn't matter how perfect

155
00:07:49,202 --> 00:07:50,603
a script you prepare.

156
00:07:51,437 --> 00:07:54,307
We cover the athletes competing

157
00:07:55,074 --> 00:07:56,943
at this moment.

158
00:07:58,444 --> 00:08:01,747
That's supposed to be our job.

159
00:08:02,715 --> 00:08:03,583
Isn't it?

160
00:08:06,886 --> 00:08:10,223
Well, no wonder a pain-in-the-neck old man

161
00:08:11,324 --> 00:08:12,792
like me gets fewer jobs.

162
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:17,563
See you.

163
00:08:24,303 --> 00:08:27,940
10,000-METER TIME TRIAL MEET

164
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:30,009
A MEET WHERE UNIVERSITY ATHLETES COMPETE

165
00:08:30,076 --> 00:08:32,245
FOR RECORDS AND PERSONAL BESTS

166
00:08:33,079 --> 00:08:35,314
-Everyone, gather round.
-Yes.

167
00:08:37,950 --> 00:08:41,320
I'll announce your legs this weekend.

168
00:08:41,921 --> 00:08:44,156
-Leg assignments…
-This is it…

169
00:08:44,223 --> 00:08:45,791
Today's 10,000-meter race

170
00:08:45,858 --> 00:08:48,528
will be a big factor in deciding them.

171
00:08:48,594 --> 00:08:51,364
Don't let up. Give it everything.

172
00:08:51,864 --> 00:08:52,732
That's all.

173
00:08:52,798 --> 00:08:53,833
-Yes.
-Yes.

174
00:08:57,737 --> 00:08:59,906
TOZAI UNIVERSITY

175
00:08:59,972 --> 00:09:01,007
SHOSUKE HIRAKAWA

176
00:09:01,073 --> 00:09:03,342
-Coach Hirakawa of Tozai University!
-Yeah!

177
00:09:03,409 --> 00:09:04,844
Mr. Hirakawa, do you have a moment?

178
00:09:04,911 --> 00:09:06,479
He's got quite a presence!

179
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:08,247
Hey, let's go get his autograph later.

180
00:09:08,314 --> 00:09:10,449
Yeah, let's go.

181
00:09:10,516 --> 00:09:12,518
Two titles in a row for sure, right?

182
00:09:12,585 --> 00:09:15,988
Still, it depends on the other teams.

183
00:09:16,055 --> 00:09:18,824
-We can't get careless.
-I see.

184
00:09:22,962 --> 00:09:24,564
Long time no see, Mr. Kai.

185
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:27,400
You all know him.

186
00:09:27,466 --> 00:09:30,036
Coach Kai of the Student United Team.

187
00:09:30,603 --> 00:09:31,437
I'm Kai.

188
00:09:32,438 --> 00:09:35,341
You two were rivals
in college, weren't you?

189
00:09:35,408 --> 00:09:36,375
No.

190
00:09:36,442 --> 00:09:40,079
We ran the same leg three times.
Izumo, All-Japan and Hakone.

191
00:09:40,146 --> 00:09:41,814
He beat me all three times.

192
00:09:41,881 --> 00:09:44,317
Calling us rivals would be presumptuous.

193
00:09:44,383 --> 00:09:46,419
But as a head coach,

194
00:09:46,485 --> 00:09:50,289
my record's a little better.

195
00:09:51,057 --> 00:09:54,226
Of course. Tozai's the reigning champ.

196
00:09:54,293 --> 00:09:57,163
This time, you'll face off

197
00:09:57,229 --> 00:09:58,731
as head coaches.

198
00:09:58,798 --> 00:10:00,399
How are you feeling about it?

199
00:10:02,401 --> 00:10:03,703
Speaking of feelings,

200
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:08,574
the Student United Team seems fired up.

201
00:10:09,141 --> 00:10:11,310
What was your goal again?

202
00:10:12,111 --> 00:10:13,512
Top three in the main race.

203
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:18,784
Be careful, Mr. Kai.

204
00:10:19,452 --> 00:10:20,786
You know the old saying.

205
00:10:21,587 --> 00:10:24,056
"A great player

206
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:26,092
doesn't always make a great coach."

207
00:10:26,158 --> 00:10:28,594
-Right?
-Yes.

208
00:10:29,295 --> 00:10:32,365
Well, go easy on us.

209
00:10:33,499 --> 00:10:34,867
Let's make it an exciting race.

210
00:10:37,236 --> 00:10:39,538
See you at Hakone.

211
00:10:43,009 --> 00:10:46,746
Next, men's 10,000-meter Heat 6.

212
00:10:50,349 --> 00:10:52,518
TOZAI UNIVERSITY
SANNO UNIVERSITY

213
00:10:52,585 --> 00:10:55,421
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY

214
00:11:26,085 --> 00:11:27,386
-Looking good!
-You got this!

215
00:11:27,453 --> 00:11:29,789
Keep that pace!

216
00:11:29,855 --> 00:11:31,157
You got this!

217
00:11:31,223 --> 00:11:33,492
Follow him!

218
00:11:35,961 --> 00:11:37,863
Come on!

219
00:11:37,930 --> 00:11:40,433
Kota and the others are flying…

220
00:11:40,499 --> 00:11:41,400
‎MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY TEAM MANAGER
‎KEITO YANO

221
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:55,781
MEISEI GAKUIN
HAKONE EKIDEN QUALIFIER

222
00:11:58,017 --> 00:12:01,987
11TH PLACE-MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY

223
00:12:02,054 --> 00:12:03,489
I'm sorry, everyone.

224
00:12:03,556 --> 00:12:05,424
It's my fault.

225
00:12:09,295 --> 00:12:10,863
Huh?

226
00:12:10,930 --> 00:12:13,232
Hayato's pace suddenly dropped…

227
00:13:07,686 --> 00:13:09,488
-Are everyone's times in?
-Yes.

228
00:13:10,823 --> 00:13:13,292
-For me…
-Man,

229
00:13:13,359 --> 00:13:15,227
I could've cut five more seconds.

230
00:13:15,294 --> 00:13:17,496
I fell behind at the end too.

231
00:13:18,230 --> 00:13:19,098
What's this?

232
00:13:19,832 --> 00:13:20,666
Huh?

233
00:13:20,733 --> 00:13:23,836
"We'll do things our way."

234
00:13:23,903 --> 00:13:26,572
These three have great times!
Especially Kota!

235
00:13:26,639 --> 00:13:28,974
-You're right.
-Isn't that weird?

236
00:13:29,041 --> 00:13:31,243
Then why is he like that at camp?

237
00:13:32,778 --> 00:13:35,614
Maybe he didn't want to get injured.

238
00:13:35,681 --> 00:13:38,050
The Student United Team has
Daichi Murai

239
00:13:38,117 --> 00:13:39,518
-from Toho Economics too.
-Yeah.

240
00:13:39,585 --> 00:13:41,020
They look pretty strong this year.

241
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:44,356
Yeah, everyone's surprisingly fired up.
Even the coach and captain.

242
00:13:44,423 --> 00:13:46,792
The captain's Mr. Aoba
from Meisei Gakuin, right?

243
00:13:46,859 --> 00:13:47,860
Oh, yeah.

244
00:13:47,927 --> 00:13:50,029
Isn't he the guy
who blew the qualifying race?

245
00:13:50,095 --> 00:13:50,963
Why is he captain?

246
00:13:51,597 --> 00:13:53,999
Well, the coach is from Meisei too.

247
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:55,868
-Right.
-Yeah.

248
00:13:55,935 --> 00:13:58,437
-That makes things easier.
-Yeah.

249
00:14:12,918 --> 00:14:15,888
Wow, this is a nice place.

250
00:14:15,955 --> 00:14:18,390
-It's got character.
-Right.

251
00:14:18,958 --> 00:14:21,660
-I guess.
-It's just old.

252
00:14:25,931 --> 00:14:27,867
Um, Mr. Karashima…

253
00:14:28,601 --> 00:14:31,437
Honestly, this broadcast is in crisis.

254
00:14:31,503 --> 00:14:32,371
YOSHIO KITAMURA

255
00:14:32,438 --> 00:14:35,474
You're the only one who can save it.

256
00:14:36,175 --> 00:14:38,611
We're sure of that.

257
00:14:40,980 --> 00:14:43,249
Right, Bureau Chief Kitamura?

258
00:14:43,816 --> 00:14:46,385
Well, they're asking this earnestly.

259
00:14:46,452 --> 00:14:48,520
-Please do it.
-No.

260
00:14:48,587 --> 00:14:49,989
Hakone and I don't get along.

261
00:14:50,789 --> 00:14:53,025
-No…
-You once said

262
00:14:53,092 --> 00:14:55,427
my directing was over the top.

263
00:14:55,494 --> 00:14:58,264
But it got ratings back then, didn't it?

264
00:14:58,330 --> 00:15:00,733
Viewers are honest.

265
00:15:01,433 --> 00:15:04,236
It's not about ratings.

266
00:15:04,303 --> 00:15:06,739
Your directing is a gimmick

267
00:15:06,805 --> 00:15:09,108
-that strays from the heart of sports.
-A gimmick?

268
00:15:09,675 --> 00:15:11,844
Watch your mouth.

269
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:12,811
Then it's a travesty.

270
00:15:12,878 --> 00:15:16,582
Um, that was 15 years ago, right?

271
00:15:17,983 --> 00:15:21,353
Let's let bygones be bygones…

272
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:25,457
Listen. I've always tried to see sports

273
00:15:25,524 --> 00:15:27,192
as sports, with no bias.

274
00:15:28,093 --> 00:15:30,095
Forcing the runners into a script

275
00:15:30,162 --> 00:15:34,099
we prepared ahead of time?

276
00:15:34,166 --> 00:15:37,303
I won't do a tame sports broadcast
like that.

277
00:15:37,369 --> 00:15:38,704
You gotta be kidding!

278
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:41,373
I'm impressed.

279
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:44,109
You're the most stubborn man in Japan.

280
00:15:44,176 --> 00:15:46,745
I don't want to hear that from you.

281
00:15:52,184 --> 00:15:55,387
-Good work.
-Good work.

282
00:15:55,454 --> 00:15:57,222
-Good work.
-Good work.

283
00:15:58,624 --> 00:16:01,627
-Good work.
-Nomura! It's been ages!

284
00:16:01,694 --> 00:16:03,929
I saw the favorite announcer rankings.

285
00:16:03,996 --> 00:16:05,464
Number one. Congrats!

286
00:16:05,531 --> 00:16:08,400
I've just been lucky with my shows.

287
00:16:08,467 --> 00:16:11,637
Famous but still humble.
I could learn from you.

288
00:16:12,972 --> 00:16:14,340
So what's up? You need me?

289
00:16:15,808 --> 00:16:16,809
Could you come with me?

290
00:16:20,546 --> 00:16:24,116
Marumaru Hour is doing great.

291
00:16:24,183 --> 00:16:25,517
It's all thanks to you, Maruta.

292
00:16:26,352 --> 00:16:31,156
Thank you. I'm really grateful
to be on such a good show.

293
00:16:33,025 --> 00:16:37,196
By the way, Maruta.
I want to ask you something.

294
00:16:37,262 --> 00:16:38,197
What is it?

295
00:16:39,431 --> 00:16:42,668
Will you be the broadcast announcer
for the Hakone Ekiden?

296
00:16:43,902 --> 00:16:45,938
What? Me?

297
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:50,576
Maeda's in the hospital,
so we're looking for a replacement.

298
00:16:50,642 --> 00:16:53,178
You started out in sports, right?
You're perfect.

299
00:16:54,947 --> 00:16:56,648
Honestly,

300
00:16:57,182 --> 00:17:00,252
I find the current
Hakone broadcast lacking.

301
00:17:00,319 --> 00:17:02,321
They pour in all those people and money,

302
00:17:02,388 --> 00:17:04,590
and it's as dull as it gets.

303
00:17:06,625 --> 00:17:07,860
Listen, Maruta.

304
00:17:08,961 --> 00:17:11,130
What we need is impact.

305
00:17:12,398 --> 00:17:15,434
An unconventional broadcast
to bring new life to Hakone.

306
00:17:16,368 --> 00:17:17,269
What do you think?

307
00:17:18,537 --> 00:17:20,172
Doesn't that sound exciting?

308
00:17:35,487 --> 00:17:38,524
Why did Bureau Chief Kitamura
even come tonight?

309
00:17:39,291 --> 00:17:42,561
How can two people get along that badly?

310
00:17:45,731 --> 00:17:47,533
Mr. Tokushige, what should we do?

311
00:17:49,301 --> 00:17:50,803
What do you think, Miyamoto?

312
00:17:52,337 --> 00:17:56,742
I still think Mr. Karashima is the
only one who can be broadcast announcer.

313
00:17:57,609 --> 00:17:59,778
Sure, he's stubborn and twisted.

314
00:17:59,845 --> 00:18:02,081
He's picky and has a nasty mouth,

315
00:18:02,147 --> 00:18:04,450
-and his ideas are old-fashioned…
-Hey, now…

316
00:18:05,884 --> 00:18:07,319
But as a sports announcer,

317
00:18:08,854 --> 00:18:10,255
Mr. Karashima has held on

318
00:18:10,322 --> 00:18:13,025
to his principles for years.

319
00:18:14,226 --> 00:18:16,762
Respect for the runners.

320
00:18:17,729 --> 00:18:19,031
I think that's what

321
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:21,266
we should value most

322
00:18:21,333 --> 00:18:24,470
when we broadcast the Hakone Ekiden.

323
00:18:28,373 --> 00:18:29,875
I think so too.

324
00:18:33,278 --> 00:18:35,481
PROGRAMMING BUREAU CHIEF
KUROISHI

325
00:18:37,049 --> 00:18:37,883
Bureau Chief Kuroishi.

326
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:43,522
Hello.

327
00:18:43,589 --> 00:18:46,258
What's happening
with the Hakone broadcast announcer?

328
00:18:47,392 --> 00:18:51,029
If it's not settled yet,
there's someone I'd like to recommend.

329
00:18:52,264 --> 00:18:53,332
Who is it?

330
00:18:54,233 --> 00:18:55,734
How about Maruta?

331
00:18:56,702 --> 00:18:57,970
Maruta?

332
00:18:58,770 --> 00:19:01,573
With a variety-show host like him,

333
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:04,510
the broadcast will be
five times more exciting.

334
00:19:05,377 --> 00:19:07,179
Will it?

335
00:19:08,013 --> 00:19:09,114
He's popular, sure, but--

336
00:19:09,181 --> 00:19:11,016
How do we get viewers to love

337
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:15,721
the Hakone Ekiden even more?

338
00:19:15,787 --> 00:19:17,456
Think hard with that thick skull of yours.

339
00:19:18,824 --> 00:19:20,659
Listen, Tokushige.

340
00:19:20,726 --> 00:19:25,464
This isn't change. It's evolution.

341
00:19:26,231 --> 00:19:28,667
Maruta's eager to do it too.

342
00:19:30,068 --> 00:19:32,171
-Mr. Kuroishi…
-Got it?

343
00:19:36,675 --> 00:19:38,377
Was that about Maruta?

344
00:19:47,753 --> 00:19:50,189
Okay. Good work.

345
00:19:53,258 --> 00:19:54,226
Thank you!

346
00:19:58,130 --> 00:20:00,832
Leg assignments are tomorrow, huh?

347
00:20:00,899 --> 00:20:02,935
I won't sleep a wink tonight.

348
00:20:03,001 --> 00:20:03,835
‎SANNO UNIVERSITY SECOND-YEAR STUDENT
‎DAN KURASHINA

349
00:20:05,137 --> 00:20:06,638
Haru, which leg did you ask for?

350
00:20:06,705 --> 00:20:07,539
HARUKA MOMOYAMA

351
00:20:07,606 --> 00:20:08,807
The seventh leg.

352
00:20:08,874 --> 00:20:10,909
Oh, same here.

353
00:20:11,677 --> 00:20:13,612
I guess that makes us rivals.

354
00:20:15,847 --> 00:20:17,049
Go…

355
00:20:17,950 --> 00:20:19,651
When some get to run,

356
00:20:20,285 --> 00:20:22,087
there are always others who don't.

357
00:20:23,622 --> 00:20:25,791
That's Hakone, right?

358
00:20:30,896 --> 00:20:32,998
Sorry, go on ahead.

359
00:20:33,599 --> 00:20:35,500
I'm going to do one more stride.

360
00:20:36,101 --> 00:20:37,202
Okay.

361
00:20:38,003 --> 00:20:39,671
-Keito, can you take this?
-Of course.

362
00:20:39,738 --> 00:20:42,040
Thanks. See you.

363
00:20:57,356 --> 00:20:59,291
Um, Coach.

364
00:21:01,193 --> 00:21:03,762
Can I ask you about something?

365
00:21:05,797 --> 00:21:07,566
It's about Hayato.

366
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:11,403
Lately, he keeps fading

367
00:21:11,470 --> 00:21:13,005
in the second half of races.

368
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:17,209
Is there anything I can do?

369
00:21:20,679 --> 00:21:23,649
Let's try it in the evening.

370
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:25,250
In the evening?

371
00:21:29,054 --> 00:21:31,423
Hayato! Wait!

372
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:34,993
Let's do a few 400s.

373
00:21:35,060 --> 00:21:36,895
-What, now?
-Yes, now!

374
00:21:36,962 --> 00:21:39,264
Oh, and take off your watch.

375
00:21:40,098 --> 00:21:41,433
Why all of a sudden?

376
00:21:42,734 --> 00:21:45,404
It feels just right!

377
00:21:48,206 --> 00:21:49,041
What does?

378
00:21:50,809 --> 00:21:51,777
First one.

379
00:21:52,444 --> 00:21:54,413
Ready, go!

380
00:22:14,499 --> 00:22:15,801
Now, the second one.

381
00:22:17,402 --> 00:22:19,137
Ready, go!

382
00:22:20,439 --> 00:22:22,040
Now, the third one.

383
00:22:23,342 --> 00:22:25,210
Ready, go!

384
00:22:58,577 --> 00:23:00,779
Hayato, that's amazing!

385
00:23:02,013 --> 00:23:03,215
Great time!

386
00:23:04,983 --> 00:23:06,218
You're right…

387
00:23:07,119 --> 00:23:09,054
It's been a while
since you ran in the 65s.

388
00:23:09,921 --> 00:23:11,456
Come to think of it,

389
00:23:11,523 --> 00:23:13,859
running felt easier than usual.

390
00:23:13,925 --> 00:23:15,627
My body felt lighter.

391
00:23:16,962 --> 00:23:19,531
Let's time it again tomorrow morning.

392
00:23:20,799 --> 00:23:22,501
-Let's do that.
-Yes.

393
00:23:29,474 --> 00:23:32,611
Did Bureau Chief Kuroishi tell you

394
00:23:33,211 --> 00:23:35,614
about the Hakone broadcast announcer?

395
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:36,581
Yes.

396
00:23:38,216 --> 00:23:41,253
I wanted to know how you feel about it.

397
00:23:44,623 --> 00:23:47,926
Honestly, I was confused

398
00:23:48,827 --> 00:23:50,028
when he first asked me.

399
00:23:50,962 --> 00:23:53,532
I wondered if I could
fill in for Mr. Maeda.

400
00:23:55,434 --> 00:23:58,036
But Mr. Kuroishi said he wants to see

401
00:23:58,103 --> 00:24:01,106
Hakone done my way.

402
00:24:03,575 --> 00:24:05,277
I plan to give Hakone

403
00:24:06,044 --> 00:24:08,980
everything I've got.

404
00:24:10,982 --> 00:24:13,652
Mr. Tokushige, I look forward
to working with you.

405
00:24:23,895 --> 00:24:24,830
Maruta.

406
00:24:25,530 --> 00:24:26,531
Yes?

407
00:24:27,098 --> 00:24:29,568
I know how good

408
00:24:30,235 --> 00:24:31,236
an announcer you are.

409
00:24:32,337 --> 00:24:33,371
Your skill

410
00:24:33,939 --> 00:24:36,374
and your flair for drawing in viewers.

411
00:24:38,844 --> 00:24:39,678
But…

412
00:24:40,178 --> 00:24:42,848
But that's exactly why I'm worried.

413
00:24:45,650 --> 00:24:47,252
As you know,

414
00:24:47,953 --> 00:24:50,922
the Hakone Ekiden runners are the stars.

415
00:24:52,390 --> 00:24:55,060
That's the principle the broadcast

416
00:24:55,126 --> 00:24:57,762
has been built on all these years.

417
00:24:59,965 --> 00:25:03,502
If you're the broadcast announcer,

418
00:25:03,568 --> 00:25:08,807
the Hakone Ekiden will surely become
Maruta's Hakone Ekiden.

419
00:25:16,481 --> 00:25:19,651
Is that a bad thing?

420
00:25:21,286 --> 00:25:25,624
TV must never change Hakone.

421
00:25:30,095 --> 00:25:31,196
Actually,

422
00:25:32,163 --> 00:25:37,702
I'm planning to ask
Mr. Karashima to be broadcast announcer.

423
00:25:45,277 --> 00:25:46,478
Okay, last one.

424
00:25:47,012 --> 00:25:48,146
I'll record the time.

425
00:25:49,447 --> 00:25:51,716
Ready, go.

426
00:26:13,772 --> 00:26:14,606
Seriously?!

427
00:26:16,775 --> 00:26:17,609
How was it?

428
00:26:17,676 --> 00:26:19,411
That's amazing! You're faster!

429
00:26:28,987 --> 00:26:30,055
Keito,

430
00:26:31,656 --> 00:26:32,924
are you stopping

431
00:26:33,825 --> 00:26:35,794
the stopwatch early?

432
00:26:37,762 --> 00:26:39,798
-I didn't stop it early today!
-Today?

433
00:26:42,701 --> 00:26:43,568
Oh, um…

434
00:26:46,204 --> 00:26:47,505
What do you mean?

435
00:26:51,443 --> 00:26:55,814
Actually, I talked to Coach Kai.

436
00:26:56,848 --> 00:26:59,818
You've been in a slump lately…

437
00:27:00,385 --> 00:27:03,688
Let's try it in the evening.

438
00:27:04,422 --> 00:27:05,323
In the evening?

439
00:27:06,157 --> 00:27:08,526
You run as it gets darker.

440
00:27:08,593 --> 00:27:11,997
What does that do?

441
00:27:13,198 --> 00:27:17,035
As it gets dark,
your field of vision narrows.

442
00:27:18,036 --> 00:27:21,473
Running like that,
you feel like you're going faster.

443
00:27:22,440 --> 00:27:23,908
It's an illusion of sorts.

444
00:27:24,442 --> 00:27:26,311
An illusion?

445
00:27:26,378 --> 00:27:29,414
Yeah. You don't actually get faster.

446
00:27:32,017 --> 00:27:32,984
And, Keito,

447
00:27:33,685 --> 00:27:37,822
stop the stopwatch
just before Hayato finishes.

448
00:27:38,890 --> 00:27:41,993
Then tell Hayato his time improved.

449
00:27:42,761 --> 00:27:45,630
-But that's--
-A bluff, of course.

450
00:27:48,033 --> 00:27:52,170
What do you think Hayato needs right now?

451
00:27:56,374 --> 00:27:58,677
Confidence, maybe?

452
00:28:01,746 --> 00:28:04,883
You give him that confidence.

453
00:28:07,519 --> 00:28:11,056
So yesterday, I stopped
the stopwatch a little early.

454
00:28:18,396 --> 00:28:22,100
But, Hayato, this time is real.

455
00:28:22,767 --> 00:28:24,769
Your time really did improve.

456
00:28:27,038 --> 00:28:30,141
Honestly, I had my doubts too.

457
00:28:31,776 --> 00:28:35,013
But it was just like Coach Kai said.

458
00:28:43,722 --> 00:28:46,024
Confidence, huh?

459
00:28:52,430 --> 00:28:53,765
Thanks, Keito.

460
00:28:54,866 --> 00:28:56,735
Sorry I made you worry.

461
00:28:58,636 --> 00:28:59,804
No!

462
00:29:00,638 --> 00:29:04,008
I'll go tell Coach Kai your time!

463
00:29:04,075 --> 00:29:06,277
Excuse me.

464
00:29:25,997 --> 00:29:27,031
Go!

465
00:29:29,134 --> 00:29:32,337
Last 5,000! Run at your own pace!
Let's pick it up!

466
00:29:32,403 --> 00:29:33,638
Don't tense up!

467
00:29:38,009 --> 00:29:39,844
SEIWA INTERNATIONAL HEAD COACH
KOICHI KITANO

468
00:29:39,911 --> 00:29:41,646
TOHO ECONOMICS HEAD COACH
SEIJIRO ONUMA

469
00:31:20,945 --> 00:31:22,413
Good work!

470
00:31:23,615 --> 00:31:24,449
Good work.

471
00:31:24,515 --> 00:31:26,784
That last surge was amazing,

472
00:31:26,851 --> 00:31:27,819
Captain.

473
00:31:30,288 --> 00:31:31,256
Thanks.

474
00:31:33,258 --> 00:31:37,462
Those three always slack off
when they train with us.

475
00:31:38,129 --> 00:31:40,265
How long are they going to keep that up?

476
00:31:49,741 --> 00:31:50,942
Got a minute?

477
00:31:55,046 --> 00:31:57,749
This team needs you three.

478
00:31:59,550 --> 00:32:01,052
So I want all three of you

479
00:32:01,653 --> 00:32:04,122
to give this team everything.

480
00:32:05,056 --> 00:32:07,325
I think you should take

481
00:32:07,959 --> 00:32:09,727
every workout seriously.

482
00:32:09,794 --> 00:32:11,496
I told you before.

483
00:32:12,797 --> 00:32:15,600
We'll do things our way.

484
00:32:16,100 --> 00:32:20,638
Just because you're captain
doesn't mean you can push your opinions.

485
00:32:31,115 --> 00:32:32,517
Thanks, Captain.

486
00:32:36,487 --> 00:32:37,956
That run was nowhere near

487
00:32:38,589 --> 00:32:41,125
what you're capable of.

488
00:32:42,493 --> 00:32:43,695
Kota, why?

489
00:32:46,397 --> 00:32:47,432
Shuto.

490
00:32:51,602 --> 00:32:52,904
Seiya?

491
00:32:55,373 --> 00:32:57,608
You slack off for no reason?

492
00:33:01,612 --> 00:33:04,582
If you train with no clear purpose
or motivation,

493
00:33:04,649 --> 00:33:06,050
don't bother.

494
00:33:06,651 --> 00:33:07,986
It's a waste of time.

495
00:33:10,088 --> 00:33:13,091
Figure out for yourselves
what kind of athletes you should be.

496
00:33:13,157 --> 00:33:15,259
And what you have to do.

497
00:33:16,995 --> 00:33:18,162
Think about it.

498
00:33:27,038 --> 00:33:29,040
I don't think the way you handled

499
00:33:29,107 --> 00:33:31,242
Kota and the others was right.

500
00:33:32,276 --> 00:33:33,311
How so?

501
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:37,548
They're much smarter than you think.

502
00:33:38,449 --> 00:33:42,286
You've been away a long time,
so you may not understand.

503
00:33:42,353 --> 00:33:46,190
Students today aren't interested
in anything unrealistic.

504
00:33:47,458 --> 00:33:48,826
Unrealistic, like what?

505
00:33:50,628 --> 00:33:52,030
I told you before.

506
00:33:52,730 --> 00:33:54,365
This team's goal.

507
00:33:56,868 --> 00:33:58,703
Why do you assume that?

508
00:34:00,238 --> 00:34:02,340
This is the Student United Team.

509
00:34:03,174 --> 00:34:04,475
Hakone isn't so easy

510
00:34:04,542 --> 00:34:06,978
that a thrown-together team can win it.

511
00:34:07,678 --> 00:34:10,681
Could you stop talking like an amateur?

512
00:34:10,748 --> 00:34:12,717
The runners know it too.

513
00:34:14,018 --> 00:34:16,421
I think the runners are on board.

514
00:34:19,057 --> 00:34:20,258
This is pointless.

515
00:34:25,096 --> 00:34:27,131
He won't get it right now.

516
00:34:27,765 --> 00:34:29,600
He's a serious man.

517
00:34:30,468 --> 00:34:33,805
But if you ask me,
he's too serious and lacks ambition.

518
00:34:34,806 --> 00:34:36,941
He relies on experience and common sense

519
00:34:37,508 --> 00:34:39,277
and never questions his assumptions.

520
00:34:41,879 --> 00:34:44,982
But Mr. Kitano was right about one thing.

521
00:34:45,850 --> 00:34:48,386
That the runners are smart.

522
00:34:50,188 --> 00:34:52,723
I'm going to bet on that.

523
00:34:53,891 --> 00:34:55,827
TOHO UNIVERSITY OF ECONOMICS

524
00:35:06,804 --> 00:35:10,408
I'll now announce your legs.

525
00:35:12,543 --> 00:35:15,546
Based on the survey, your times,

526
00:35:16,180 --> 00:35:18,950
stamina and strengths,

527
00:35:19,016 --> 00:35:20,485
I've given each of you

528
00:35:21,052 --> 00:35:23,554
two possible legs for now.

529
00:35:23,621 --> 00:35:25,490
-Two?
-Why?

530
00:35:25,556 --> 00:35:26,791
What do you mean?

531
00:35:30,094 --> 00:35:32,363
LIST OF LEGS

532
00:35:32,430 --> 00:35:34,398
The fourth leg and the tenth leg…

533
00:35:34,465 --> 00:35:36,400
Yes! I got the first leg!

534
00:35:36,467 --> 00:35:38,836
The fifth leg! Time to climb the mountain!

535
00:35:38,903 --> 00:35:39,837
You're loud.

536
00:35:39,904 --> 00:35:44,509
By the end of December,
I'll decide the ten who'll run.

537
00:35:44,575 --> 00:35:46,544
As soon as you can,

538
00:35:47,111 --> 00:35:49,180
walk the course you'll run.

539
00:35:49,247 --> 00:35:50,248
JO INOMATA

540
00:35:50,314 --> 00:35:51,916
Study the course closely.

541
00:35:52,483 --> 00:35:54,785
The feel of the town. The road surface.

542
00:35:54,852 --> 00:35:58,623
Know the buildings at each kilometer.
Drill it into your heads.

543
00:35:58,689 --> 00:36:01,559
Where the turns are, how the wind blows,

544
00:36:01,626 --> 00:36:02,527
the ups and downs.

545
00:36:02,593 --> 00:36:03,261
‎MAKOTO AMAGI
‎FIRST AND EIGHTH LEGS

546
00:36:03,327 --> 00:36:04,662
Note the sun's direction

547
00:36:04,729 --> 00:36:06,864
and how warm it gets.

548
00:36:06,931 --> 00:36:07,565
‎REN MINEGISHI
‎THIRD AND TENTH LEGS

549
00:36:07,632 --> 00:36:10,868
Then make your own race plan

550
00:36:10,935 --> 00:36:12,904
and figure out where it'll be decided.

551
00:36:12,970 --> 00:36:13,671
‎FUTA WADA-SECOND AND FIFTH LEGS

552
00:36:13,738 --> 00:36:16,007
Knowing the course inside out

553
00:36:16,574 --> 00:36:18,876
makes all the difference in the main race.

554
00:36:18,943 --> 00:36:20,278
KOTA MATSUKI
FIRST AND NINTH LEGS

555
00:36:20,344 --> 00:36:21,746
Picture how you'd run it

556
00:36:22,313 --> 00:36:24,148
and where you'd make your move.

557
00:36:24,215 --> 00:36:26,517
Imagine and simulate it.

558
00:36:27,084 --> 00:36:28,252
One plan isn't enough.

559
00:36:29,020 --> 00:36:31,022
Picture several scenarios

560
00:36:31,989 --> 00:36:33,824
and think it through deeply.

561
00:36:34,725 --> 00:36:35,893
-Yes.
-Yes.

562
00:36:41,265 --> 00:36:42,800
You two just won't give up.

563
00:36:43,467 --> 00:36:45,102
Why don't you ask Maruta?

564
00:36:46,537 --> 00:36:48,072
If we use Maruta,

565
00:36:48,839 --> 00:36:50,741
the Hakone Ekiden will change.

566
00:36:50,808 --> 00:36:53,010
He's adaptable enough.

567
00:36:53,077 --> 00:36:56,280
If he's asked, he'll fit in.

568
00:36:57,281 --> 00:36:59,350
Sappy directing is right up his alley.

569
00:37:00,151 --> 00:37:01,252
Mr. Karashima.

570
00:37:01,752 --> 00:37:06,357
We want to see the Hakone Ekiden
with you calling it.

571
00:37:07,258 --> 00:37:08,893
We want viewers to see

572
00:37:08,960 --> 00:37:12,363
Dainichi TV's proudest Hakone Ekiden

573
00:37:12,964 --> 00:37:14,532
through Bunzo Karashima's eyes.

574
00:37:21,105 --> 00:37:24,508
"A sports broadcast announcer
should be a traffic light."

575
00:37:25,810 --> 00:37:28,980
Mr. Maeda kept those words in mind

576
00:37:29,046 --> 00:37:31,449
as Hakone's broadcast announcer.

577
00:37:31,949 --> 00:37:34,619
Car One is with the leaders.
How's Aoyama Gakuin looking?

578
00:37:34,685 --> 00:37:35,586
Mr. Okada?

579
00:37:35,653 --> 00:37:38,656
Igarashi of Aoyama Gakuin
is slowing a little…

580
00:37:38,723 --> 00:37:40,224
Over to Car Two for a moment.

581
00:37:40,291 --> 00:37:43,494
From the studio, he directs traffic
like a traffic light.

582
00:37:44,061 --> 00:37:47,198
He gets the announcers in the field to say

583
00:37:47,265 --> 00:37:48,766
the right things at the right time.

584
00:37:49,634 --> 00:37:51,302
"Don't make yourself the focus."

585
00:37:51,369 --> 00:37:55,706
"Let the right person deliver
the most important information."

586
00:37:56,674 --> 00:37:59,343
"Mr. Karashima was the one
who taught me that."

587
00:38:00,378 --> 00:38:03,114
That's what Mr. Maeda said.

588
00:38:07,985 --> 00:38:10,021
We absolutely need you

589
00:38:10,655 --> 00:38:13,858
to make the Hakone Ekiden a success!

590
00:38:18,262 --> 00:38:19,797
Can I say something?

591
00:38:22,433 --> 00:38:23,301
Maruta…

592
00:38:30,908 --> 00:38:31,976
Mr. Karashima.

593
00:38:37,081 --> 00:38:41,185
Will you be the broadcast announcer
for the Hakone Ekiden?

594
00:38:45,289 --> 00:38:47,992
Mr. Kuroishi wants it to feel

595
00:38:48,059 --> 00:38:49,226
like a variety show.

596
00:38:50,695 --> 00:38:51,595
But…

597
00:38:52,563 --> 00:38:55,866
I know the Hakone Ekiden
isn't that kind of broadcast.

598
00:38:57,835 --> 00:39:00,705
I did start out in sports, after all.

599
00:39:03,341 --> 00:39:05,443
Mr. Tokushige, you told me, right?

600
00:39:06,944 --> 00:39:08,979
TV must never change Hakone.

601
00:39:11,515 --> 00:39:13,284
I agree.

602
00:39:15,419 --> 00:39:18,055
No more and no less.

603
00:39:19,123 --> 00:39:23,194
I'm not the one who can show
the Hakone Ekiden as it is.

604
00:39:24,695 --> 00:39:26,030
You are.

605
00:39:30,101 --> 00:39:33,971
I'm not ready to take Hakone's sash yet.

606
00:39:47,284 --> 00:39:50,755
Mr. Karashima, please.

607
00:39:53,057 --> 00:39:56,227
Honestly,

608
00:39:56,761 --> 00:39:59,797
getting drilled for two hours

609
00:39:59,864 --> 00:40:01,665
on my name in training was rough.

610
00:40:02,967 --> 00:40:03,801
But

611
00:40:04,635 --> 00:40:08,072
I still remember what you told me.

612
00:40:09,607 --> 00:40:11,809
"Your name is your calling card."

613
00:40:12,376 --> 00:40:14,545
"You have to say it better than anyone."

614
00:40:17,047 --> 00:40:20,785
I'm really grateful
you were so strict with me.

615
00:40:22,086 --> 00:40:24,488
I want to learn from you again

616
00:40:25,523 --> 00:40:28,192
at Hakone.

617
00:40:30,161 --> 00:40:31,529
Mr. Karashima.

618
00:40:32,830 --> 00:40:34,565
I'm asking too.

619
00:40:34,632 --> 00:40:36,133
Please.

620
00:40:40,137 --> 00:40:41,138
Please.

621
00:40:55,953 --> 00:41:00,257
ANNOUNCING DEPARTMENT

622
00:41:12,102 --> 00:41:15,005
-Mr. Tokushige, do something!
-What?

623
00:41:15,072 --> 00:41:17,842
That's right. We need him to say yes!

624
00:41:18,409 --> 00:41:20,411
Don't blame me!

625
00:41:21,245 --> 00:41:23,113
I'm trying too!

626
00:41:32,223 --> 00:41:34,758
-Tokushige.
-Yes?

627
00:41:35,659 --> 00:41:36,794
Do you have it? That thing.

628
00:41:38,863 --> 00:41:40,631
That thing. Don't you know?

629
00:41:41,866 --> 00:41:43,467
The handbook.

630
00:41:44,034 --> 00:41:46,871
The Hakone Ekiden Broadcast Handbook.

631
00:41:50,975 --> 00:41:52,843
Get it to me by tomorrow.

632
00:41:54,445 --> 00:41:55,412
Okay.

633
00:41:58,048 --> 00:41:59,483
Well, I'm going to eat.

634
00:42:03,687 --> 00:42:04,989
Thank you!

635
00:42:06,790 --> 00:42:10,728
-Yes!
-Thank goodness…

636
00:42:21,472 --> 00:42:23,941
That was close.

637
00:42:25,876 --> 00:42:28,479
I'm sorry about Hakone.

638
00:42:32,082 --> 00:42:37,488
I just think Mr. Karashima
should be the broadcast announcer.

639
00:42:39,323 --> 00:42:40,157
I see.

640
00:42:43,494 --> 00:42:45,596
Well, it can't be helped.

641
00:42:46,297 --> 00:42:50,234
Let's both pray it's a good show.

642
00:42:52,436 --> 00:42:53,337
Yes, sir.

643
00:42:54,572 --> 00:42:55,506
Excuse me.

644
00:43:00,611 --> 00:43:02,513
MARUMARU HOUR
BY SHINJI MARUTA

645
00:43:12,957 --> 00:43:13,891
Good work.

646
00:43:14,592 --> 00:43:15,726
Good work.

647
00:43:16,460 --> 00:43:18,796
What's this? It's upside down.

648
00:43:18,862 --> 00:43:20,497
You're right.

649
00:43:31,508 --> 00:43:35,446
HEAD COACH'S OFFICE

650
00:43:35,512 --> 00:43:36,447
Come in.

651
00:43:37,348 --> 00:43:38,449
Excuse me.

652
00:43:41,552 --> 00:43:42,686
Did you see this?

653
00:43:48,726 --> 00:43:49,727
MONTHLY TRACK &amp; FIELD MAGAZINE

654
00:43:49,793 --> 00:43:51,629
-Huh?
-I knew it would

655
00:43:51,695 --> 00:43:53,397
come to this someday.

656
00:43:54,064 --> 00:43:56,867
I only agreed to coach

657
00:43:56,934 --> 00:43:59,503
because we placed
13th in the qualifying race.

658
00:44:00,170 --> 00:44:01,271
That's it.

659
00:44:03,040 --> 00:44:04,842
Why do I have to waste every weekend

660
00:44:04,908 --> 00:44:07,444
on this ridiculous training?

661
00:44:08,946 --> 00:44:09,813
Um…

662
00:44:11,148 --> 00:44:14,652
what should I do
about practice starting next week?

663
00:44:14,718 --> 00:44:16,820
Decide that yourself.

664
00:44:18,122 --> 00:44:19,156
But

665
00:44:19,223 --> 00:44:23,227
if you don't go, I won't either.

666
00:44:27,598 --> 00:44:28,465
COACH SHOSUKE HIRAKAWA

667
00:44:28,532 --> 00:44:32,136
"Abolish the Student United Team"?

668
00:44:33,671 --> 00:44:36,840
What's the point of letting

669
00:44:36,907 --> 00:44:39,510
a Student United Team
with no official record compete?

670
00:44:41,111 --> 00:44:43,514
Instead of adding a team like that,

671
00:44:43,580 --> 00:44:46,250
they should let another strong school run.

672
00:44:46,316 --> 00:44:48,819
At this point, it's just laughable.

673
00:44:55,392 --> 00:44:56,226
45 DAYS UNTIL HAKONE EKIDEN

674
00:44:56,293 --> 00:44:57,327
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
UNRELATED TO REAL PEOPLE OR GROUPS.
